WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.219
Who can read the logs, and for how long.

2
00:00:02.499 --> 00:00:07.747
Treat logs and traces that contain user content as production data, because they are.

3
00:00:08.027 --> 00:00:24.133
The OWASP cheat sheet’s guidance on protecting logs applies directly: restrict who can read them, review those privileges periodically, record and monitor access to the logs themselves, protect them against tampering, use secure transport when they cross networks,

4
00:00:24.413 --> 00:00:27.357
and keep them for the required period and no longer.

5
00:00:27.637 --> 00:00:39.925
A structure that works for LLM systems is two tiers: Metadata tier: ids, versions, token counts, latency, cost, status, pseudonymous user ids, redaction counts.

6
00:00:40.205 --> 00:00:45.773
Broadly readable by the engineering team, retained long enough for trend analysis (often months).

7
00:00:46.053 --> 00:00:47.867
This is what your dashboards query.

8
00:00:48.147 --> 00:01:02.483
Content tier: redacted prompts and outputs, captured only where policy allows, in a separate store with its own access list (named reviewers, on-call during an incident), short retention (days to weeks), and access logging.

9
00:01:02.763 --> 00:01:05.813
Spans and metadata records point to it by id.

10
00:01:06.093 --> 00:01:10.083
This is the external-storage pattern from the semantic conventions.

11
00:01:10.363 --> 00:01:12.880
Retention needs an owner and a mechanism.

12
00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:16.531
Set time-to-live on every store at creation, not “later.

13
00:01:16.811 --> 00:01:33.109
” Make deletion requests reach every tier: if a customer exercises the right to erasure under GDPR (Article 17), the request has to find their pseudonymous records, their content in the content tier, and any copies in eval datasets.

14
00:01:33.389 --> 00:01:44.589
Keeping the HMAC key lets you compute the pseudonym for a known user to find their rows; deleting the key is one way to make old pseudonyms unlinkable, if your policy chooses that.
